+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-rejects-holes-and-non-json-values
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch rejects holes and non-JSON values"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 requires `value` to be a JSON value. `applyPatch` only checked that the member existed, and
+`Array.prototype.map` skipped holes in a sparse patch array.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate `value` of `add`, `replace` and `test` as JSON (null, boolean, string, finite number, array,
+plain object, recursively) and visit every patch slot with `Array.from`, so holes are rejected as
+non-object operations. Validation still happens before any operation is applied.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Patches that were silently accepted now throw; valid patches are unaffected.
