+id: task-003-make-applypatch-validation-conform-to-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Make applyPatch validation conform to RFC 6902"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## What was done
+
+Reviewed `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 by probing each operation, edge cases and error paths. Two
+invalid patches were accepted: an operation slot that is a hole in a sparse array (skipped by `map`),
+and an `add`/`replace`/`test` whose `value` is not JSON (e.g. `undefined`, `NaN`). Both now throw
+before any operation is applied. Tests added in `test/patch.test.ts`. The other behaviours checked
+(add/move/copy/test semantics, array indexes, `-`, move into own child, atomicity) already conform.
